#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175725 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176064 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41472e46-65d2-579b-85b7-309749ed3a5f" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Trinomial Whose Terms Have a Common Factor"}] :question/id #uuid "2ed3f2e8-2d0e-59e0-a9dc-1856245b768c" :question/math-academy-id "e-1343" :question/problem "Factor $3x^2 - 21x + 30$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can factor out a $3$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x^{2} - 21x + 30 &=  \\\\\n&= 3(x^{2} - 7x + 10)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial $x^2-7x+10$ in parentheses.\n\nWe start by listing the factor pairs of the constant term $(10)$, but only the negative factor pairs since the coefficient of the linear term $(-7)$ is negative.\n\n$$\n(-1,-10), (-2,-5)\n$$\n\nNow we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(-7)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}(-1) + (-10) &= -11 & \\cdot \\\\ (-2) + (-5)|=-7 & ✓\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, we write the linear term as $-7x=-2x-5x$, and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 7x + 10 &=  \\\\\nx^{2} - 2x - 5x + 10 &=  \\\\\n(x^{2} - 2x) + (-5x + 10) &=  \\\\\nx(x - 2) - 5(x - 2) &=  \\\\\n&= (x - 5)(x - 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3\\left(x^2-7x+10\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= 3(x-5)(x-2) \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175797 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d960485-d99c-555f-abb6-8e4d0564913e" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Trinomial With a Negative Quadratic Term"}] :question/id #uuid "1c852599-e08e-5b54-be2b-700c3f8f47f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-6931" :question/problem "Factor the expression $-2x^2-22x-48$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can factor out a $-2$ from each of the terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x^{2} - 22x - 48 &=  \\\\\n&= - 2(x^{2} + 11x + 24)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the polynomial $x^2+11x+24$ in parentheses.\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(24)$:\n\n$$\n(1, 24), (2, 12), (3, 8), (4, 6)\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $(11)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 + 24 &= 25 & \\cdot \\\\ 2 + 12|= 14 & \\cdot \\\\ 3 + 8|= 11 & ✓ \\\\ 4 + 6|= 10 & \\cdot\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified in the previous step, write the linear term as\n\n$$\n11x=3x+8x\n$$\n\nand then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -2\\left(x^2+11x+24\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= -2\\left(x^2+3x+8x+24\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= -2\\left((x^2+3x)+(8x+24)\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= -2\\Bigl(x(x+3)+8(x+3)\\Bigr) \\\\[5pt] &= -2(x+8)(x+3) \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175949 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d960485-d99c-555f-abb6-8e4d0564913e" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Trinomial With a Negative Quadratic Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92a52351-b0ea-5214-b447-eb8bfc25cede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174919} {:answer/id #uuid "c44caa58-b68e-5fc5-ae37-46ffc70f9415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174920} {:answer/id #uuid "e5830896-5bea-546f-8950-0461dcc18f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174921} {:answer/id #uuid "e88abefb-6bda-5f3c-9741-77dfe56290a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174922} {:answer/id #uuid "3ddace94-63fa-5071-994a-652bc14cb466" :answer/ty